# Build output.
/target

# Editors and the things a desktop leaves behind. None of these are anybody
# else's business, and all of them have been committed to a repository before.
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store

# Instruction files that assistant tooling writes into a checkout are not
# listed here, and cannot be: naming one would put a tool's name in a tracked
# file, which is the thing `.githooks/no-attribution` exists to stop — it
# fails on this file if you try. They do not need listing. Such a file says
# in its own contents what wrote it, so the same check refuses the commit,
# and that check is the one CI runs and nobody can opt out of.
#
# Keep them out of the working tree, or under /scratch below.

# Scratch. A directory for working files that are not the work.
/scratch/
